([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?::(([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?)?)|[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?:[0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f]([0-9A-Fa-f])?)?)?::))\])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
    </data>
  </define>
  <define name="kind.vendor">
    <a:documentation>CPU vendor: Exactly 12 printable ASCII characters (space to ~) with no comma, such as AuthenticAMD or GenuineIntel, kept as written with no white space stripped; or an empty element, which is a value of its own (state no vendor) and not the default.</a:documentation>
    <data type="string">
      <param name="pattern">([ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-][ -+.-~\-])?</param>
    </data>
  </define>
  <define name="kind.blocksize">
    <a:documentation>block size: 512 or 4096, a number of bytes in ASCII digits; white space round it is ignored. No sign, no underscore, no leading zero and no unit. An empty element is an error.</a:documentation>
    <data type="string">
      <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*(512|4096)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
    </data>
  </define>
  <define name="devices">
    <element name="devices">
      <a:documentation>Lists the vfio-user servers every guest gets, one &lt;server&gt; each; replaces the three per-VM device counts. No attributes, no text; at least one &lt;server&gt;. Later layers merge entries by id, append new ids and cannot remove one. Every guest gets the same list.</a:documentation>
      <mixed>
        <oneOrMore>
          <ref name="server"/>
        </oneOrMore>
      </mixed>
    </element>
  </define>
  <define name="server">
    <element name="server">
      <a:documentation>One device server every guest gets; its children set that server's backend, config file or options. Requires type and id, and takes no other attribute. Children allowed depend on type; each may appear once unless the option is repeatable. Kind of server: an ernic NIC, a rocjitsu GPU, an SDXI device or an SPDK NVMe controller. ernic, rocjitsu, sdxi or spdk. The generator refuses more than one spdk a guest, and an spdk with no &lt;spdk-image&gt;. An id cannot change type in a later layer.</a:documentation>
      <choice>
        <group>
          <attribute name="type">
            <value type="string">ernic</value>
          </attribute>
          <ref name="server.id"/>
          <mixed>
            <interleave>
              <optional>
                <element name="backend">
                  <a:documentation>Sets an ernic NIC's RDMA backend; any type but tcp takes that NIC out of the generated TCP mesh. ernic only. Text is the backend's own options, optional, as one word with no whitespace: size=1G,ns=2,kv=1,size=256M. The parser checks only that; tcp takes none.</a:documentation>
                  <choice>
                    <group>
                      <attribute name="type">
                        <a:documentation>Which RDMA backend the NIC's server runs. none, loopback, tcp, nvmeof or s3. Required on &lt;backend&gt;, and its only attribute.</a:documentation>
                        <value type="string">tcp</value>
                      </attribute>
                      <data type="string">
                        <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                      </data>
                    </group>
                    <group>
                      <attribute name="type">
                        <a:documentation>Which RDMA backend the NIC's server runs. none, loopback, tcp, nvmeof or s3. Required on &lt;backend&gt;, and its only attribute.</a:documentation>
                        <choice>
                          <value type="string">none</value>
                          <value type="string">loopback</value>
                          <value type="string">nvmeof</value>
                          <value type="string">s3</value>
                        </choice>
                      </attribute>
                      <data type="string">
                        <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                      </data>
                    </group>
                  </choice>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="log-level">
                  <a:documentation>Log verbosity of this NIC's server. none, error, warn, info or debug; the server's default is warn. The parser does not check the word.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <zeroOrMore>
                <element name="nic-profile">
                  <a:documentation>Shapes the NIC from a profile; repeatable, and later profiles win. A built-in name (compat, small-vm, generic-100g, generic-400g) or a path to an ini file inside the server container. Repeatable, order kept; a later layer naming it replaces all earlier values.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </zeroOrMore>
              <optional>
                <element name="stats-interval-ms">
                  <a:documentation>How often the server rewrites the guest's statistics; overrides every profile. Milliseconds, 10 to 60000; the server's default is the profile's, 1000. The parser does not check the number or range.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="eth-queues">
                  <a:documentation>Number of Ethernet Rx/Tx queues the NIC offers the guest; overrides every profile. Integer 1 to 64; the server's default is the profile's, 4. The guest uses at most one per vCPU. The parser does not check the number or range.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <zeroOrMore>
                <element name="inject">
                  <a:documentation>Injects a fault into this NIC's server, for testing; repeatable. One fault as 'SITE: PATTERN effect EFFECT', for example 'stats_vals: every 100 effect fail status eio'. Spaces allowed. Repeatable, order kept; unchecked by the parser.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </zeroOrMore>
            </interleave>
          </mixed>
        </group>
        <group>
          <attribute name="type">
            <value type="string">rocjitsu</value>
          </attribute>
          <ref name="server.id"/>
          <mixed>
            <interleave>
              <optional>
                <element name="config">
                  <a:documentation>Names the rocjitsu simulation config file for this one GPU, in place of &lt;rocjitsu-config&gt;. rocjitsu only. One file name in the image's configs directory, no path: starts with a letter or digit, then letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'. Example gfx1250_mi455x.json.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._\-]*)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="node">
                  <a:documentation>Selects one local node from a rocjitsu system manifest; needed for a multi-node launch. A node name from the manifest the config file refers to; unchecked by the parser.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="cpu-thread-budget">
                  <a:documentation>Overrides the CPU thread budget of this GPU's server; zero selects automatic sizing. Integer count of threads; 0 is automatic. The parser does not check that it is a number.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="wait-checking">
                  <a:documentation>Overrides this GPU server's wait checks. off disables checks, on enables ordinary checks, all adds the gfx1250 XCNT checks. The parser does not check the word.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;]([^\t\n\r&#x7F;&#x85;&#x2028;&#x2029;]*[^\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;&#x7F;])?)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
            </interleave>
          </mixed>
        </group>
        <group>
          <attribute name="type">
            <value type="string">sdxi</value>
          </attribute>
          <ref name="server.id"/>
          <mixed>
            <zeroOrMore>
              <element name="verbose">
                <a:documentation>Raises the SDXI server's log verbosity; repeat it for debug output. A switch: empty element, no value, no attributes. May be repeated; each occurrence renders one --verbose.</a:documentation>
                <data type="string">
                  <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                </data>
              </element>
            </zeroOrMore>
          </mixed>
        </group>
        <group>
          <attribute name="type">
            <value type="string">spdk</value>
          </attribute>
          <ref name="server.id"/>
          <mixed>
            <interleave>
              <optional>
                <element name="namespaces">
                  <a:documentation>The namespaces the SPDK NVMe controller serves, in order; sets the image's NVME_NAMESPACES. One word, comma list, NSIDs in list order: lba:malloc:SIZE[:BLOCK], lba:aio:PATH[:BLOCK[:SIZE]], kv:mem[:MAXVAL[:MAXKEYS]]. Image default lba:malloc:512M,kv:mem.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([A-Za-z0-9_.:,/=\-]+)[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="serial">
                  <a:documentation>Serial number of the SPDK NVMe controller, as the guest sees it; sets the image's SPDK_SERIAL. 1 to 20 letters, digits, '_' and '-'. Image default SPDKVFU01.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*([A-Za-z0-9_\-]{1,20})[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
              <optional>
                <element name="cpumask">
                  <a:documentation>Host cores the SPDK server's poll-mode reactor spins on; sets SPDK_CPUMASK. Each server takes one full core. Hexadecimal core mask, 0x then 1 to 32 hex digits, such as 0x4. Default 0x1, host CPU 0. One value for every guest's server, so guests share the cores it names.</a:documentation>
                  <data type="string">
                    <param name="pattern">[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*(0x[0-9A-Fa-f]{1,32})[\t\n\r &#x85;&#xA0;&#x1680;&#x2000;-&#x200A;&#x2028;&#x2029;&#x202F;&#x205F;&#x3000;]*</param>
                  </data>
                </element>
              </optional>
            </interleave>
          </mixed>
        </group>
      </choice>
    </element>
  </define>
  <define name="server.id">
    <attribute name="id">
      <a:documentation>Names the entry for later layers to merge on and for error messages; does not rename containers or sockets. Starts with a letter; letters, digits, '_', '.' and '-'; 32 characters at most; unique in the block.</a:documentation>
      <data type="string">
        <param name="pattern">[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_.\-]{0,31}</param>
      </data>
    </attribute>
  </define>
</grammar>
